## 2. Age requirement

Include only patients who were:

- **Age ≥18 years at the date of the first qualifying eGFR measurement within the study window.**

Use date of birth and the actual specimen collection date of the first qualifying eGFR.

Do not determine age using the end of the study period.

## 3. CKD identification must be laboratory based

Identify CKD using **reported estimated GFR derived from serum/plasma creatinine**.

Search all available laboratory tables for creatinine-based eGFR results.

Prefer structured laboratory component names, LOINC/component identifiers, or clearly labeled eGFR fields.

Include only eGFR measurements that are clearly based on **serum/plasma creatinine**.

Do not use:

- ICD codes
- Problem lists
- CKD diagnosis fields
- Billing diagnoses
- Urine creatinine
- Creatinine clearance
- Measured GFR
- Cystatin-C-only eGFR
- Combined creatinine-cystatin C eGFR unless it can be clearly separated from creatinine-only eGFR
- eGFR values calculated during dialysis treatments

If several creatinine-based eGFR equations are present, identify the equation/type when available and report it. Do not silently combine clearly incompatible eGFR result types.

## 4. Require chronicity

A patient qualifies only if there are **at least TWO valid creatinine-based eGFR measurements <60 mL/min/1.73 m² within the defined 60-month study window and separated by at least 90 days**.

Both values must satisfy:

`eGFR <60 mL/min/1.73 m²`

