## 7. Laboratory quality control

- Use **specimen collection date/time** for determining whether the eGFR falls within the 60-month eligibility window.
- Do not use result-posting time when specimen collection time is available.
- Deduplicate repeated laboratory records representing the same specimen.
- Exclude cancelled, corrected-invalid, or erroneous laboratory results when identifiable.
- Standardize eGFR units to `mL/min/1.73 m²`.
- Do not interpret an eGFR reported only as `>60` as qualifying CKD.
- If an eGFR is reported as `<15`, retain the categorical information but do not invent an exact numeric value.
- Keep the original laboratory value and original unit for audit purposes.

